   "made": "2026-09-30T18:04:15.501Z"
  },
  "02": {
   "text": "In seventeen-oh-one, missionary Joachim Boo-vay sent the mathematician Leibniz a diagram from China.",
   "model": "eleven_v4",
   "voiceId": "hYDmtgsUa8Lf6Ql57aI5",
   "settings": {
    "stability": 0.5,
    "similarity_boost": 0.75,
    "style": 0,
    "use_speaker_boost": true
   },
   "seconds": 7.28,
   "sha256": "80ad30aa84b32fc2a475a175e75898691f8ac0102d5eb3d4446ad3f883d98aa8",
   "made": "2026-09-30T18:04:19.332Z"
  },
  "03": {
   "text": "Leibniz already counted using only zeros and ones.",
   "model": "eleven_v4",
   "voiceId": "hYDmtgsUa8Lf6Ql57aI5",
   "settings": {
    "stability": 0.5,
    "similarity_boost": 0.75,
    "style": 0,
    "use_speaker_boost": true
   },
   "seconds": 4.24,
   "sha256": "fb4fd029ffbb0b0ec31bdd40d3450ece3a3cd4133746596da5ba8ef174bd98f3",
   "made": "2026-09-30T18:04:21.407Z"
  },
  "04": {
   "text": "Here, broken means zero; solid means one. The patterns count from zero to sixty-three.",
   "model": "eleven_v4",
   "voiceId": "hYDmtgsUa8Lf6Ql57aI5",
   "settings": {
    "stability": 0.5,
    "similarity_boost": 0.75,
    "style": 0,
    "use_speaker_boost": true
   },
   "seconds": 8.16,
   "sha256": "05c6993178fc563120e37dd5bc0de008cc57f6ffaa5861df3e256b16108f5d34",
   "made": "2026-09-30T18:04:26.126Z"
  },
  "05": {
   "text": "He was delighted. His paper credited the figures to the legendary Foo Shee.",
   "model": "eleven_v4",
   "voiceId": "hYDmtgsUa8Lf6Ql57aI5",
   "settings": {
    "stability": 0.5,
    "similarity_boost": 0.75,
    "style": 0,
    "use_speaker_boost": true
   },
   "seconds": 5.68,
   "sha256": "5a93df8c6eab761a4b33028c610f229c91daa604f5a4e6c13cdd5b0ac567dd15",
   "made": "2026-09-30T18:04:30.222Z"
  },
  "06": {
   "text": "The order is attributed to Shaow Yong, an eleventh-century scholar.",
   "model": "eleven_v4",
   "voiceId": "hYDmtgsUa8Lf6Ql57aI5",
   "settings": {
    "stability": 0.5,
    "similarity_boost": 0.75,
